course: dictionary
lesson: 2736
title: Who is in charge?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. «The director chooses who fits each part» means the person who runs a film or play, not someone who points the way.
explain: Look for clues about the job. In the sentence «The director decides how it should look and feel», the words decides and look tell you the director is in charge of how the film or play appears.
explain: The words after director often tell you what they lead. «The director of music» leads music, and «the board of directors» is a group who run a company. Each one is a person in charge of something.
fact: A director is the person in charge of making a film, play or TV programme.
fact: A director tells the actors and crew what to do.
fact: A director is also one of the people who run a company or a large organisation.
fact: A take is one try at filming a shot, and directors often film many takes to get it right.
fact: The crew are the people behind the camera, including camera, sound, set and costume teams.
exercise: «In an audition people try out, and the director chooses who fits each part.» What does the director do in this sentence? | *Chooses who gets each part | Builds the costumes and sets | Eats lunch with the actors | Sells the tickets
exercise: «After a show the director gives praise and notes.» What are notes here? | Music for the stage | Tickets sold at the door | Money paid to the actors | *Small changes to make it better next time
exercise: In the phrase «the director of music», what kind of person is the director? | A person who sells tickets | An actor who plays a small part | *The head of a department | A camera operator
test: «A take is one try at filming a shot.» What is a take? | A whole film | *One try at filming a shot | A costume worn by an actor | A seat in the cinema
test: «The crew are the people behind the camera.» Who are the crew? | The actors on the stage | *The people who record, build and make the film | The people who buy tickets | The audience watching the show
exam: «The director decides how it should look and feel.» What does the director decide? | Where the cinema is | How much the tickets cost | What time the show starts | *How it should look and feel
